---
description: Never leave Cursor Co-authored-by trailers on git commits or PRs
alwaysApply: true
---

# No Cursor commit attribution

Do not add `Co-authored-by: Cursor`, `cursoragent@cursor.com`, or `Made with Cursor` to commits or PRs. The authored subject (and body, if any) is the whole message.

The environment may append this trailer even when you omit it. That still counts as adding it. After every `git commit`:

1. Run `git log -1 --format=%B`
2. If the message contains `Co-authored-by: Cursor`, rewrite HEAD with `git commit-tree` (not `git commit --amend`, which can re-inject it)
3. Confirm the trailer is gone before you finish

```
# BAD
Keep enquiry details after a failed form submission

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>

# GOOD
Keep enquiry details after a failed form submission
```
